1. Country Model Class

The Country class is a simple Java Bean (POJO) used to store country information such as country code and country name.

Features
Contains two private variables: code and name.
Includes both default and parameterized constructors.
Provides getter and setter methods to access and modify data.
package com.cognizant.springlearn.model;

public class Country {

    private String code;
    private String name;

    public Country() {
    }

    public Country(String code, String name) {
        this.code = code;
        this.name = name;
    }

    public String getCode() {
        return code;
    }

    public void setCode(String code) {
        this.code = code;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }
}
2. CountryList Configuration Class

The CountryList class acts as a container for storing multiple Country objects. It is registered as a Spring Bean using the @Component annotation.

Features
Stores a list of countries.
Provides getter and setter methods.
Automatically managed by the Spring Container.
package com.cognizant.springlearn.service;

import java.util.List;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import com.cognizant.springlearn.model.Country;

@Component
public class CountryList {

    private List<Country> countries;

    public List<Country> getCountries() {
        return countries;
    }

    public void setCountries(List<Country> countries) {
        this.countries = countries;
    }
}
3. Country Service

The Service Layer contains the business logic. It fetches the list of countries from CountryList and returns the details of India.

Features
Annotated with @Service.
Uses @Autowired for Dependency Injection.
Searches for the country whose code is "IN".
package com.cognizant.springlearn.service;

import java.util.List;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import com.cognizant.springlearn.model.Country;

@Service
public class CountryService {

    @Autowired
    private CountryList countryList;

    public Country getCountryIndia() {

        System.out.println("Inside Service");

        List<Country> countries = countryList.getCountries();

        for (Country country : countries) {
            if (country.getCode().equalsIgnoreCase("IN")) {
                return country;
            }
        }

        return null;
    }
}
Explanation
@Service → Marks the class as the Service layer.
@Autowired → Injects the CountryList bean.
Returns the country object whose code is "IN".
4. Country Controller

The Controller Layer receives HTTP requests and calls the service layer.

Features
Annotated with @RestController.
Maps the URL /country.
Returns a Country object as JSON.
package com.cognizant.springlearn.controller;

import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;

import com.cognizant.springlearn.model.Country;
import com.cognizant.springlearn.service.CountryService;

@RestController
public class CountryController {

    @Autowired
    private CountryService countryService;

    @RequestMapping("/country")
    public Country getCountryIndia() {

        System.out.println("Inside Controller");

        return countryService.getCountryIndia();
    }
}
URL Mapping
GET http://localhost:8083/country
Sample Response
{
    "code":"IN",
    "name":"India"
}
5. Spring XML Configuration (country.xml)

The XML file creates and initializes the CountryList bean with predefined country data.

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<beans xmlns="http://www.springframework.org/schema/beans"
       xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.springframework.org/schema/beans
       http://www.springframework.org/schema/beans/spring-beans.xsd">

    <bean id="countryList"
          class="com.cognizant.springlearn.service.CountryList">

        <property name="countries">

            <list>

                <bean class="com.cognizant.springlearn.model.Country">
                    <property name="code" value="IN"/>
                    <property name="name" value="India"/>
                </bean>

                <bean class="com.cognizant.springlearn.model.Country">
                    <property name="code" value="US"/>
                    <property name="name" value="United States"/>
                </bean>

                <bean class="com.cognizant.springlearn.model.Country">
                    <property name="code" value="JP"/>
                    <property name="name" value="Japan"/>
                </bean>

                <bean class="com.cognizant.springlearn.model.Country">
                    <property name="code" value="DE"/>
                    <property name="name" value="Germany"/>
                </bean>

            </list>

        </property>

    </bean>

</beans>
Purpose
Creates the CountryList bean.
Loads four country objects.
Injects the list into CountryList.
6. Main Application Class

This is the entry point of the Spring Boot application.

package com.cognizant.springlearn;

import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.ImportResource;

@SpringBootApplication
@ImportResource("classpath:country.xml")
public class SpringLearnApplication {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        SpringApplication.run(SpringLearnApplication.class, args);

    }
}
Explanation
@SpringBootApplication → Starts the Spring Boot application.
@ImportResource → Loads the country.xml configuration file.
SpringApplication.run() → Initializes the Spring Container and starts the embedded server.
